  "notes": "GAAP city. Governmental lines from the Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balance, Total Governmental Funds column (p4: General, Permanent Trust, Street, Keno). Business-type (Water, Sewer, Golf) from the Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Net Position total column (p6); no single total printed, so receipts = total operating revenues + interest income and disbursements = total operating expenses + interest expense. Utility cost-type lines use the cost type as category with function utilities (total column includes Golf). Governmental charges for services 238,353 are all Parks and Recreation per the Statement of Activities (p2), so Recreation Fees. Beginning fund balance 1,277,326 with restatement (126,024) as an adjustment (restated 1,151,302). Ending cash = cash 17,203 + CDs 40,000 + county treasurer 7,018 from the governmental funds balance sheet (p3); restricted cash/CDs excluded. Balance sheet = government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1), Primary Government Totals column; component units (Parkview Lodge, Airport Authority) ignored. Detail: the only supplementary schedule is the combined all-funds budgetary statement (p9), so per the 2026-10-27 per-fund rule detail is one line per fund column of the governmental funds (p4) and proprietary funds (p6) statements; p9 not recorded. Many 1-dollar rounding differences in the printed statements are listed in report_discrepancies. Read pages 1-9 of 9"
